    }
  ],
  "clarifying_question": null,
  "summary": "You should use the Thermogravimetric Analyzer (EQ17) rather than the DSC (EQ18) to find the decomposition temperature of your drug-polymer blend. TGA is specifically designed to measure mass loss during degradation, whereas decomposing a sample inside a DSC risks permanently contaminating the sensitive heat-flow sensor with off-gassed volatiles. Run TGA first to establish the degradation onset, and then use that safe upper temperature limit for your booked DSC run to study melting or glass transitions."
}

