  "summary": "To inspect cells in 6-well plates while maintaining sterility for passaging, you need an inverted microscope that images through the bottom of the plate rather than an upright microscope. The Keyence BZ-X810 (EQ09) is ideal if you want automated well scanning and software-based confluence and cell counting, while the inverted Nikon TE300 (EQ13) and Olympus IX83 (EQ23) are well suited for routine visual confluence checks and manual hemocytometer counting. Note that counting unstained cells directly in the well can be inaccurate at high confluence or in dense stem cell colonies, so confirming phase-contrast optics and a 6-well plate holder on your chosen system is recommended."
